        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Head-margin note set into a break in the long rule that brackets the household, population, outcaste, shrine, temple, village and shizoku columns, printed sideways in half-size type: \"surveyed on the second day of the tenth month of the kōgo year\" — Meiji 3, i.e. 1870. The rule runs rightward to the head of the 戸數 column and hooks downward there; a short rule closes the bracket on the left, above the 士族 column."
